A||N||65||Formula88||Your first car?||||5||
Z||000000||Formula88||11-15-2001||06:47 PM||||So, tell us the story about your first car.  <P>Mine was a '69 Firebird 350 I got in High School.  Faded beige paint, missing vinyl roof, 2-speed automatic and a 2 barrel carb.  By the time I sold it, it had a Turbo350 tranny, quadrajet, bright red paint with gold pinstripes, and true dual exhaust with Sonic Turbo Mufflers, Moroso chrome air cleaner and all braided steel hoses.  MAN, that was a fun car!  I bought my second car, a 72 Trans Am shortly after High School (still had the 69).  Talk about an ego trip.  I'd walk outside and say, hmmm, which one of my bad a$$ cars do I want to drive today?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <P>I kept the T/A all original, since it was so rare.  Then the new car bug bit me, and I sold the '69 to get the down payment on a new '87 Grand National (that's dates me a bit, huh?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">)  The GN was fun, and fast as He!!.  I put in a 160* thermo and Kenne-Bell Hi-Lo Pro chip.  That chip alone must have added about 40HP.  Before you call  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_bs.gif"> remember, the chip upped the boost from about 12psi to 19psi.  <P>Anway - fast forward to about 2 years ago.  I run into a friend of mine I used to work with at the movie theatre and he tells me he knows the guy how currently owns my old 69 Firebird, and it's for sale!  Woo Hoo!  So I beat feet out to look at the car and nearly cried when I saw her.  Sitting in his front yard just rotting away.  Exactly like it was when I sold it, but with about 12 years of weather and neglect added.  Still, I wanted to rescue her.  She still started and drove, but the tranny was leaking from sitting so long.  Then comes the bad news.  Some idiot who owned between me and the current owner decided to go 4-wheeling in it and ran over a tree stump!  Ripped a hole in the rear end.  The owner said he replaced the rear end with a 10-bolt out of an old Nova 6 cylinder, so it supposedly had 4.10 gears, now.  And to top it off, he wanted $2500 for it!  The car was worth about $300-500 in it's current condition, but he knew it was my first car (no, I didn't tell him, my "friend" did).  If it hadn't been for the rear end damage, I probably would have paid the $2500 just to have her back.  But there was no way to know how bad the rear subframe and unibody was damaged.  Too many unknowns.  But that's ok.  About a year after that, I found my Fiero Formula.  I wouldn't have been able to get my Fiero if I'd bought the Firebird, so it's all good.  <P>Still, I keep thinking about riding back out to the country to see if she's still sitting there.  A part of me keeps hearing her calling to me.  <P>Now, selling my 72 Trans Am?  THAT was a mistake.  But I did it to finance college.  I would love to find another 72 Firebird to make a TA replica out of so I could mod the heck out of it and not worry about originality.  Maybe someday.  Right now, my Fiero gets all my attention (and money!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">)<P>So, that's my story.  What about yours?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Jay||11-15-2001||06:51 PM||||My first car was a 1980 LADA!  My grandfather painted it black for me, but it was actually more like dark brown. LOL.  It died about a year later infront of a dealership.  Outside was an 84se.  So I left the Lada at the side of the road and bought the 84.  Sold it the next summer, about 8 years later I bought the 86 GT and as they say the rest is history...<P>------------------<BR>Jay<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/newsig2_copy_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Kasdan||11-15-2001||06:55 PM||||My first car was a black 1990 Chevy Lumina Euro.  2 door, 16 inch allor wheels, wrap around spoiler, 3.1 the previous owner had turbo'ed, very fun car.  Automatic, headlight and tail light blackouts, quad exhaust.  Man, i wish i had put that motor in my fiero  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Tyler Morgan, 1986 GT<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/kassig2.gif">                  <BR>Aftermarket Power Steering, Rebuilt 2.8<BR>http://www.geocities.com/mtyler14/index.html||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroKyle||11-15-2001||06:58 PM||||My first car is mty current 85 GT. Celebrated my 1 year anviersary last weekend. Has it been that long already? Its already unfortunatly been to the body shop twice because of accidents. One night I left it out of gear and it rolled 10 feet into a tree on flat pavemebnt over night. Then 5 weeks ago I was broadsided in it. But its all good now as all the damage is fixed, and half the car has new paint. So it looks much better then when I first got the car because the front end was in dire need of paint. Then about 6 weeks ago I purchased a 85' Buick Regal. Its not bad conddition, no body rust, and runs great. Wish is was the T-type, but its just a winter beater. Also its really good for parties. Don't care what happens to it and it has bench seats for sleeping up to 2.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> So thats all my cars and their stories so far, and I am only 16. Haha. I look for a better future for my current 85. I want the Archie Special in it down the raod, until then, just keeping it mint and low miles.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://communities.msn.com/_Secure/0PgAgVMwT!1W9RUb20vChbvv6QaE!2K1LWrFB6SxTnTchZgvIygv7Y3YwXpVdD8GeNkWpurYfoQxvNRK6j6kEmOFLoIHavbIr/Kyle-85-GT.jpg">    <P>My Fast 'n Black Car<BR>Kyle - 85' GT||||reg||1
Z||000004||WampusCat||11-15-2001||07:04 PM||||My first car was a '61 Fiat 1100 sedan bought for $150 in '77.  It had a 4 on the tree shifter and suicide doors.  My poor father spent almost every weekend working on that thing and was really happy when I sold it and bought a '71 Pinto for $250.  I drove the Pinto for 2 1/2 years with no big problems and sold it for $150.||||reg||1
Z||000005||baptistheart||11-15-2001||08:11 PM||||My first car was a 1968 chevy two door hardtop impala with a 327 not to bad, but compared to todays cars it was a monster.<P>------------------<BR>Joe||||reg||1
Z||000006||Rodrv6||11-15-2001||08:13 PM||||My first car was a 66 Barracuda Formula S that my dad gave me when I was a senior in high school.  He bought it new in 66 and gave it to me in 76.  It had a "Commando" 273 cu.in. V8 with a dual point distributer and a Carter 4 bbl carb.  It also had front disc brakes, limited slip differential, quick ratio manual steering, and was an automatic.  It was pretty quick and a real blast to drive <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>I sold the car in 1985 for $1,000 to a fellow in Tennessee.  It was still in near original condition and was an excellent candidate for a restoration.  I had too many other toys or I'd of kept it myself.  I've since found out that Plymouth only made about 3500 Formula S's in 66, so I really regret not having kept it!!!!!<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  <BR>White 88 GT :)||||reg||1
Z||000007||Return of Fiero||11-15-2001||08:23 PM||||My first car was a black 88' 2.5 Fiero. Shortly after I bought my second car, another black 88' 2.5 Fiero, hence, I called them "The Twins". The first one my father paid to have it kitted with a lotus engine (i never did anything to the thing, it always went to the dealer, even for tune ups) and the beefed up suspention. My friend decided to blow it up on the highway, and last i knew, it was at Car World in Candia NH. then there was one, who i didnt have time for, and all it needed was a clutch. it sat with the new clutch in the drivers seat for a few months, then my parents had it removed,(bone yard) with a new clutch in the cab. last i knew, the clutch was put in, and the car was sold. I miss the twins.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> DAMN PARENTS!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif"><BR>Myke||||reg||14
Z||000008||MrPBody||11-15-2001||09:11 PM||||A 1964 <A HREF="http://home.att.net/~cochrans/jagmk201.htm" TARGET=_blank>Jaguar 2.4 MkII</A> saloon (sedan).  It taught me to be a mechanic.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000009||Brian87egotrip||11-15-2001||09:21 PM||||a 76 vette.  ok ok it was a cheVETTE. Thing sounded like a vacum cleaner coming down the road.  what a monster that car was. zero to sixty in 2.5 minutes if I was going down hill 3.5 if uphill.  CHICK MAGNET <P>------------------<BR>Brian                    87GT||||reg||1
Z||000010||California Kid||11-15-2001||09:26 PM||||'65 Pontiac Tempest Coupe 326 auto. Worked at a Pontiac Dealership part time during high school. In the first year I put in a hot cam, shaved 389 tripower heads (relieved the cycl bores for valve clearance), hi flow alum intake with "jutted" AFB 4 bbl, headers/cherry bombs, and dual point distributor. Beefed the trans swapping shim plates for more clutch plates. GTO's, no problem!!!  Also cost me my license about a year after the modifications, because I was young, and dumb. Had a lot of fun, never any tickets during drag racing, only the cruises home doing 5 to 10 over.<P>Man, I wish I had known the guy above who sold that Barracuda Formula S.  Those are awesome even today. ||||reg||1
Z||000011||Sage||11-15-2001||09:28 PM||||1956 Buick...road TANK! Looked really good.<BR>Car-$50.00<BR>Trans Rebuild-$300.00<BR>Mechanical experience gained-priceless.<P>------------------<BR>Have a good one!||||reg||1
Z||000012||Cooter||11-15-2001||10:03 PM||||A 1967 LWB Chevy fleetside pickup. Worn out 350 and a saginaw 4 speed. The truck was a support vehicle from an airforce base fire crew and was bright yellow very early in its life, but when I had it the paint was more like yellow chalk. I drove it through most of high school until I got my imatation '73 RS/Z-28 Camaro on the road. Now, that was a scary car! Well built 327 (hit 7000 rpms with it several times), t-5 OD tranny and 3.07 rear end gears, I would not want to know how fast that car would have gone.||||reg||1
Z||000013||maryjane||11-15-2001||10:30 PM||||'64 Ford 6 cyl, auto, 4 door City of Houston<BR>police car. $200 at auction. No radio, no a/c, no nuthin. They scraped the police emblem off the doors with a razor scraper. a million miles on the odometer. My father bought my twin brother & myself each one. My brother used his to drag a '56 Belair with a v8 out of the pasture it had been sitting in for ten years and went to work on it. Used mine to drive to downtown Houston Marine recruiter. Joined up, left that day for MCRD, never saw the car again.||||reg||1
