Z||000049||FieroMontreal||11-16-2001||10:06 PM||||My first car was an 86 Fiero GT.. I bought it about 2 years ago.. at the time I was 14.. Car hasn't been on the Road since '97 .. I have my liscence now but I am unable to drive it yet because it is not road worthy.. at the moment.. I already sunk $3000 since I bought it.. not inc the cars purchase price.. I guess I have about 1000-2000 left to put in  the car.. Looks really nice though! I'm the second owner, Looks mint inside and pretty damn good outside.. only damage is on the decklid.. I hope to get it out next summer!<P>Since then I've also owned<P>84 Fiero SC... was nice.. blew the head gasket and was later used as a parts car<P>84 Fiero 2M4 ... Busted Frame, got a refund  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigfieromontreal_1.gif">  <BR>1986 Fiero GT, STOCK Wingless, <BR>-Alex President of FieroMontreal... <A HREF="http://www.fieromontreal.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fieromontreal.com</A> <BR>and Regional Director of CFOG-I for Eastern Canada.||||reg||1
Z||000050||GarethWright||11-17-2001||03:34 AM||||My First car was a '91 Geo Prism that my dad gave me when I got my license, I gave it to my sister when she got hers.<BR>The First car I bought myself was a 1970 1/2 Ford Falcon (although I was looking for Fieros at the time)<BR>I sold that and (not seeing any local Fieros for sale) got a summer off work and a Geo Metro Convertable, that let water in through the roof.  I traded That for a 1976 MG Midget (loved that car, taught me most of what I know about mechanicing, rear-ended by Jeep Grand Cherokee)<BR>Then with the insurance money, I got my 87 GT!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GarethsSig2.GIF"> ||||reg||1
Z||000051||Master_Sushi||11-17-2001||03:51 AM||||My first car was a white 1988 Pontiac Lemans 4 door 5 speed. Not a bad car, ya it was slow and didn't handel well. No wait... It was a terrable car  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">. lol It got me where I was going.<P>My first real car was my 88 coupe. I wish I still had it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">. That thing was mint and worth way more then I got for it. O well! Such is life.<P>I'm now on my black84se beater. I am either going to get an import this spring, or a mint fastback GT. Whichever I decide on I hope it to e my best car yet  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">.||||reg||10
Z||000052||deceler8||11-17-2001||10:21 AM||||1970 1/2 Camaro. Pretty much downhill since, but reversed the slide with my '86 coupe.<P>The '86 reminds me of the Camaro more than any car I've ever driven. Has the same great handling and head turning looks. But I wish I still had the 350 that was in that Camaro.||||reg||1
Z||000053||Tonker||11-17-2001||01:38 PM||||86 Sunbird. It was a piece of crap... For the money I ended up dumping on that thing, I could have bought a Fiero.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>My second was an 84 GMC Jimmy, when I was about 19. Firetruck red - just like the chief's truck, actually. My friends and I were on the way to the mall one day when one of them noticed a firetruck behind us with its lights on, but no siren. I pulled over, as I'm suposed to, to let him through and he pulls in behind me(???). So I look in the rearview to see what's going on and nothing.. they're just sitting there looking at us. My friend, in the passenger seat, sticks his head out the window to see what they're doing and all of a sudden they start looking panicked... They must have thought that they were following the firechief's truck or something.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> So I drop the truck in gear spin the back end a bit and ride off into the sunset... looking for the mall and some more naive firefighters.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000054||avengador1||11-18-2001||06:25 PM||||My first car was a 70 1/2 Firebird Espirit with a 2 barrel 350 V-8 and a shot powerglide tranny for $350. I got another tranny from the junkyard for $25 out of a Camaro. The bell housing bolt pattern was different so I transferred the guts from one tranny to the other. I lost the exhaust sytem behind the y pipe after going over some rail road tracks (car was real low to the ground). I bought a cherry bomb and put it were the original exhaust had broken off. I drove the car for about six months before selling it for $500. I sure miss it. You could be doing 70 M.P.H. and drop it into low and mash the pedal and it would peel out and go to 100 before upshifting.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
